# All four AMASS levels back to back inside ONE block. The block's steps are
# pre-multiplied <<3 once by the producer; each segment divides by its own
# amass_level, so the physical step count must come out identical whichever
# level the segment used. This is the vector that catches a shift applied to
# the wrong operand or at the wrong time.
gvec 1
name amass-levels
f_tick 16000000
pulse_ticks 160
pos 0 0 0

blk 1 800 800 800 800 0x00 0x00
seg 4 1999 1 0 0
seg 8 999 1 1 0
seg 16 499 1 2 0
seg 32 249 1 3 0
